# In-development → Changelog

When you change a prototype whose `manifest.json` `status` is `in-development` (or `ready-for-dev`), **always** add a Changelog to-do after the change — do not wait for the user to ask.

## When this applies

- Editing files under `mocks/` for a prototype with that status
- UX copy, layout, interaction, or flow changes meant for engineering

Skip trivial fixes (typos in comments, formatting-only) unless the user asks.

## What to do

1. Confirm the prototype id from `data-prototype-id` / `manifest.json`.
2. After committing the mock change (or with it), create a changelog item:

```bash
node scripts/add-changelog.mjs --id <prototype-id> --title "Short change title" --summary "What developers should build or update."
```

3. Title: imperative, specific (e.g. `Rename Modify Filters to Search for more`).
4. Summary: enough for a developer — where in the UI, what changed, why.
5. Status defaults to `todo` (developer marks done in Changelog UI).
6. Screenshots/annotations are optional for agent-created entries; mention in the summary if a visual annotation would help.

## Do not

- Ask “should I add this to the changelog?” when status is in-development — just add it
- Create changelog entries for prototypes with status `active` or `draft` unless the user asks
- Skip the script if Supabase isn’t set up; still run it (it falls back / reports errors clearly)
